Scheduled Tasks: 
Tasks running as SYSTEM with modifiable executables or weak permissions.

Sample commands: 
schtasks /query /fo LIST /v to list tasks; 
check permissions with icacls <task_path>


## View Scheduled Tasks
schtasks /query        Basic List of All Scheduled Tasks
schtasks /query /fo LIST /v      Detailed List of All Scheduled Tasks
schtasks /query /fo LIST /v | findstr /i "Run As TaskName Action"      Pipe to findstr to filter
schtasks /query /fo LIST /v | findstr /i "SYSTEM Administrator"        Search for high-privilege tasks
Get-ScheduledTask    Powershell list All Tasks
Get-ScheduledTask | Where-Object {$_.Principal.UserId -match "SYSTEM|Administrator"} | Select TaskName,Principal,Actions      Powershell Combine with filters for privilege escalation hunting
Get-ScheduledTask | Get-ScheduledTaskInfo | Select TaskName,LastRunTime,NextRunTime,LastTaskResult,NumberOfMissedRuns   Powershell Detailed Task Info 
Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName "TaskName" | Get-ScheduledTaskInfo    Get information about specific task
Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName "TaskName" | Select -ExpandProperty Actions      Look for tasks that recently ran or are about to run, and check their actions
Get-ScheduledTask | Get-ScheduledTaskInfo | Where-Object { $_.LastRunTime -gt (Get-Date).AddMinutes(-10) } | Select TaskName, LastRunTime, LastTaskResult, NumberOfMissedRuns    Lists tasks where LastRunTime is within the last 10 minutes.
Get-WinEvent -LogName Microsoft-Windows-TaskScheduler/Operational -FilterXPath "*[System/TimeCreated[timediff(@SystemTime) <= 600000]] and *[System[(EventID=200 or EventID=201)]]" | Select TimeCreated, Id, Message | Format-List      Queries the Task Scheduler operational log for events in the last 10 minutes (600,000 ms)
